  "behavior": [
    "Actual BaseListStorage lives in stable shared storage. ListObserver reads its canonical size/head/tail directly under a short lock; there is no detached metadata mirror.",
    "BaseList detach_removal/finish_removal phases are shared by raw engine removal and typed List. Typed removal releases the metadata borrow and lock before user Drop; normal destructor observes native intermediate fields.",
    "Clear leaves canonical native metadata intact throughout normal destruction, then resets it. Panic cleanup resets actual metadata before remaining owned items unwind.",
    "ListNativeCursor owns canonical current/previous state; ListCursorObserver reads it during destruction. Removal updates current after destruction, matching native observation. Existing Copy ListCursor is preserved.",
    "Native cursor next/removal resolve live owner pointers before dereference, retaining fresh allocation provenance after incremental-arena address reuse.",
    "Move and exchange transfer metadata between stable logical owner states; source observer handles see empty state after native move rather than following moved nodes.",
    "Miri validates normal and panic observation, original topology, borrowed iteration, ownership, and a destructor spawning/joining a cross-thread metadata observer with no lock retained across user code."
  ],
